      "writtenOn": "2025-09-08T19:11:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`copyExternalImageToTexture` in Blink has [its own validation](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgpu/gpu_queue.cc;l\u003d718;drc\u003daba14550ed0b4620deb59e7c5f551cbde8970fb3) of the destination format.\n\n`CopyTextureForBrowser` is not part of the spec, so it doesn\u0027t need to follow any spec. IMO, there\u0027s no harm in supporting every format that it\u0027s trivial to do so (every format that doesn\u0027t require extra code to support). (Technically, it\u0027s part of Dawn\u0027s non-standard public API, but I doubt it\u0027s used outside Chromium.)\n\nPlus, we might go ahead change the spec for `copyExternalImageToTexture` to accept all renderable formats, in which case we\u0027ll need to do this anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "cf88b732_0ac384a2",
